<title>VENEZUELA: RESEARCH ALERT-Vencemos buy.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Vencemos buy.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caspian Research said it had raised its year-end price target for Venezuelan cement company Vencemos's Type I shares to 1,300 bolivars from 1,043.</p>
<p>-- said: &quot;Vencemos is one of only a few investment vehicles available with which to participate in Venezuelan's expected infrastructure boom over the next three to five years&quot;.</p>
<p>-- said: &quot;Vencemos is still among the cheapest cement stocks in Latin America on a cash flow valuation basis&quot;.</p>
<p>-- noted that recent payment of two stock dividends had raised total shares outstanding to 545 million shares from 300 million.</p>
<p>-- Vencemos is a subsidiary of Mexican cement group Cemex SA</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
